++# Claim
++
++At `8ae1e84` (pull request vasiloglou/dev-tools#51, on `origin/main` `31249da`), `changed`
++and `review` read one set of fields to decide whether an entry was read, `changed --strict`
++exits 1 while a component's `reread:` line is left and 0 on a subsystem's, and the two
++`process-phase` texts send the answer to a `reread:` line into the entry. The six gates
++above ran on that commit with the exits shown.
++
++**This record was written after the code.** Both commits were made and pushed before it
++existed. It is a retrospective record of what happened, not the record of a phase run
++under `process-phase`. "What the lane requires and this change does not have", below, lists
++what is missing.
++
++## Why there is a record
++
++`.devtools/project.md` ("Which lane a piece of work takes") puts "a change to what a gate
++refuses" in the evidence lane, as a milestone. `changed --strict` now refuses what it
++accepted before. The change was made as a fix with a pull request and no record. The
++owner was then asked whether it needs a milestone record and ruled that it does.
++
++## The owner's words
++
++These are the only approvals. Each was typed in the session that started this one and
++relayed to this session on 2026-11-26; this session did not see them typed.
++
++| The owner said | In reply to | What it covers |
++|---|---|---|
++| "you should file a detailed issue and then start fixing it" | the findings that became issue 50 | filing issue 50 and starting the fix |
++| "go og" (read as "go on") | a recommendation to keep `--strict` failing on a component's unanswered `reread:` line, with subsystem lines advisory | the `--strict` decision and the subsystem decision below |
++| "create a milestone record" | "Does the dev-tools gate change need a milestone record, or do you accept it as a fix?" | this record |
++
++None of them is a ruling on a plan or a spec at a digest, so none is written above as a
++`ruling:` gate. No plan gate, no owner gate on a spec and no close ruling took place.
++
