++## Decisions
++
++| Decision | What was chosen | Why | Who |
++|---|---|---|---|
++| Which fields say an entry was read | `does`, `verbs`, `flow`, `reread`: the narrower of the two rules, the one `review` already had | An edit to `notes`, `tests` or `modules` does not say the description was read. Of the issue's 103 listed entries, 14 had only such fields edited | Proposed by issue 50; implemented as proposed |
++| Where an unanswered `reread:` line fails | Under the existing `--strict`, not under a new flag | The two shipped places that run the check (`examples/components-check.yml`, the milestone `process-phase` gate) already name `--strict`; a new flag would leave every existing gate silent until each project edited it | Recommended to the owner; "go og" |
++| Whether a subsystem's line fails | It does not. It is printed and is advice | A project with many subsystems that share common components would have to answer most of its subsystems on every code change, and the answers would become rote | Recommended to the owner; "go og" |
++| The text of the line | `entry not edited` kept where nothing was edited | The capture in `docs/components.html` shows that line, and it stays true | This session |
